From d0d03dccd26bc3ef4970bab093e3fe6b86762bdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 16:07:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CPU monitor: measurement version of v12 (Settings > CPU
 monitor)

Off after every power-up. While on:
- measures each call of AudioEngine::routine() with OS timer 0 (33.33 MHz,
  free running since the task manager started it; only read): render time
  over the audio time rendered, average and busiest call, per half second
- counts voices (now, max), cpuDireness (max, share of the audio rendered
  above 0), voices the CPU guard really cuts short (each once: a cull call
  that leaves its voice as it was, or hits one already fading fast or
  stopped, doesn't count), SD sample cluster reads (count; average and
  longest read time, both as wall clock and without the audio routine
  calls that ran while the read waited for the card) and the longest gap
  between two calls
- OLED: one inverted line at the bottom, drawn on top of the finished
  image in a canvas of its own, new twice a second
  ("C43/71% V24 D0 S2.4/9", SD without the audio meanwhile);
  7-segment: short "C 43" popup every 2 s
- sends the per-second numbers as SysEx F0 00 21 7B 01 10 ... F7 (format 2,
  in cpu_stats_core.h) only on USB MIDI port 3 to the computer, never DIN,
  and only while the USB send buffer has room

No sound changes: the audio routine is kept whole in routineUnmeasured()
(its machine code is the same as v12's routine() apart from data offsets)
and routine() only wraps it; while off, the wrapper costs one flag test.
cullVoice() only gains the counter, its choices are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
